BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hoosier EVA at Bloomington Farmer's Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261010T123000
UID:534c400ad85f8a81461e256515c8e607@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/290e
 448/2147483647/strip/true/crop/900x546+0+0/resize/254x154!/quality/90/?url
 =https%3A%2F%2Fmedia.ndew.org%2Fe%2Fe-5381-ghuzwizr.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Hoosier EVA\nAt the Bloomington Community Farmers
 ’ Market\, we're excited to welcome neighbors\, families\, and curious v
 isitors to stop by and learn more about the growing world of electric tran
 sportation. Our booth will be hosted by the newly reformed Hoosier Electri
 c Vehicle Association in Bloomington\, a local group that’s reconnecting
  EV owners\, supporters\, and anyone interested in cleaner\, quieter ways 
 to get around our community. The market takes place at Showers Common next
  to City Hall\, a familiar gathering place where Bloomington comes togethe
 r every week to shop\, talk\, and share ideas. And don't forget A Fair of 
 the Arts\, also happening then.\n We’ll have friendly\, straightforward 
 information about electric vehicles\, hybrids\, electric bikes\, and the p
 ractical benefits of making transportation more efficient and more sustain
 able. Whether you’re already driving electric\, thinking about your next
  vehicle\, or just curious about how EVs fit into everyday life in Bloomin
 gton\, we’d love for you to stop by\, ask questions\, and join the conve
 rsation. If we have an electric bike on hand\, it will be a great way to s
 ee another side of local electric mobility up close.\n Our goal is not jus
 t to share information\, but to build a community around transportation ch
 oices that work better for people\, neighborhoods\, and the future of Bloo
 mington. Come meet local EV enthusiasts\, learn from real-world experience
 s\, and discover how electric transportation can fit into daily life\, whe
 ther that means driving\, biking\, or simply exploring new options.
LOCATION:Fernandez Plaza in front of Bloomington City Hall\, 401 N. Morton
  St.\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47404
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/hoosier-eva-at-bloomingto
 n-farmers-market-02-10-2026-16-59-25
