ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/112a
 5b7/2147483647/strip/true/crop/801x801+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb8%2F45%2F3ee0facc49ef86ec
 d0474a5aa3b7%2Fsst-logo-web-info.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by WonderLab Science Museum\nScience Story Time is g
 eared toward listeners toddler through early elementary ages. This program
  uses children’s picture books to engage as well as support scientific c
 oncepts and experiments. Young scientists develop literacy and STEM skills
  as well as build vocabulary by actively participating in the hands-on pro
 gram. Activities designed for ages 2-6. All are welcome. Activities vary m
 onthly.\nTickets: https://wonderlab.org/
