 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fac%2Fe8%2Fe40945974fc18e
 4570b7d96936cc%2Face-ukulele-class-flyer.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by The Arts Federation\nJoin us for a fun\, 8-week c
 lass designed for adults who are new to the ukulele\nor looking to build a
  strong foundation.\nNo prior musical experience is required. Bring your o
 wn ukulele or lend\none from TAF at no cost!\nIn this class\, you'll:\n•
  Learn foundational ukulele skills and basic chords\n• Explore beginner-
 friendly songs and playing techniques\n• Learn the basics of music theor
 y\n• Build confidence playing the ukulele\n Instructor: Olivia Sutherlin
 \nOlivia Sutherlin is a multidisciplinary musician with a lifelong backgro
 und in\nthe performing arts\, including theater\, choir\, and band.\n Loca
 tion: The Arts Federation (638 North St\, Lafayette\, IN 47901) - Recordin
