BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginning Watercolor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261028T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261028T143000
UID:3b61c2d7b2788851c5f86c901be92401@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/9eee
 ef7/2147483647/strip/true/crop/500x282+0+0/resize/254x143!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F1b%2Fae%2Fe6c03cdb46b382f5
 b26f7f717625%2Fclass-2466-1.jpg
DESCRIPTION:This introductory watercolor class with award-winning artist a
 nd instructor\, Mary Sue Veerkamp Schwab\, is packed full of helpful infor
 mation for beginner level students. Whether you paint along with the instr
 uctor or work on your own\, you can expect individual attention and will b
 e amazed at what you can do! \n Class Objectives:\n- Review of the basics:
  What can my brushes and paper do for me?\n- Wet-on-Wet: Applying wet pain
 t to a pre wetted paper to create a soft blend for skies and florals. \n- 
 Wet-on-Dry: Applying paint directly to dry paper for a sharp controlled ed
 ge. \n- Layering watercolor with watercolor (transparent washes) \n- Use l
 ayering and dry brush on small compositions to hone skills \n This class w
 ill include demonstrations and students participate in supportive classroo
 m critiques. Many students request taking this class a second or third tim
 e! \n Supplies: The following materials are based on Mary Sue's painting a
 pproach\, and are suggestions\, not requirements. Students are welcome to 
 incorporate their own material preferences\, and must bring their own supp
 lies:\n Paper:\nThe most important element. Arches cold press paper is rec
 ommended\, in block or sheet formats.\n- Block\, 140pound\, Cold Press\, 9
 x12 or 10 x14 or 11x14.\n- Large individual sheets\, can be divided into 2
 -4 smaller sheets\, buy Cold Press.\n Paints:\nI recommend a limited palet
 te. 10 Winsor & Newton Professional grade colors:\n- 6 warm colors: Winsor
  Red\, Winsor Yellow\, Burnt Siena\, and Raw Siena\, Permanent Rose and Wi
 nsor Violet.\n- 4 cool colors: Winsor Blue Green Shade\, Winsor Blue Red S
 hade\, Hookers Green\, and Paynes Grey.\n Other items:\n- Dr. Ph. Martin's
  Bleed Proof White Fine Art Paint\, or similar opaque white.\n- Pencils\, 
 hard lead 2H or 4H\n- *Pencil sharpener\n- Kneaded eraser\n- *Drawing boar
 d\, 12"x26"\n- White watercolor tape (not painter's tape)\n- Palette and m
 ixing pans (preferred is ceramic white palette)\n- *2 small water holders 
 or cups\n- Small mixing pans for colors\, mine have lids.\n*Drawing boards
 \, pencil sharpener\, paper towels\, rulers\, and water holders/cups will 
 be available\, but you may use your own if preferred.\n Brushes:\nDo not s
 pend a fortune on brushes. Winsor & Newton has an inexpensive line. I also
  like the black silver brushes.\nSizes: 1” and ½”flat\; #4 or #7 #10 
 round\; Detail #2 round. Must have a couple of large watercolor brushes fo
 r washes. My favorite brush: Silver Black Velvet Oval ¾”.\n Supplies ca
 n be ordered from several art suppliers including Blick\, Jerry's Artarama
 \, or Bloomington Fine Arts Supply if you prefer to shop locally.\nTickets
 : ivytech.edu/cll
LOCATION:Ivy Tech Community College Bloomington (Center for Lifelong Learn
 ing)\, 200 Daniels Way\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47404
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/beginning-watercolor-24-0
 8-2026-11-07-20
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Symphonic Band – Eric M. Smedley\, conductor
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261028T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261028T213000
UID:a570d744f96e381f33c4fadabbf39307@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/6f3d
 913/2147483647/strip/true/crop/240x180+0+0/resize/254x191!/quality/90/?url
 =http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Ffe%2F9e%2F7bfd0fe2490eaeee
 be23d54f8c07%2F8375-smedley-eric-2021fa-webcal-js-rev-1628114112.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Featuring graduate student conductor Anthony McDonnell\n Reper
 toire\nJoseph Turrin: Academy Overture (2017)\nBenson: The Leaves are Fall
 ing (1964)\nCorey Chang: What’s Next? (2024/25\, premiere\, D.M. dissert
 ation)\nJoni Greene: AfterGlow (2024)\nJodie Blackshaw: 22° halo (2022)\n
 Alfred Reed: Russian Christmas Music (1944/69)\n About the Conductor\n Eri
 c M. Smedley is associate professor of music in bands at the Indiana Unive
 rsity Jacobs School of Music\, where he directs the Symphonic Band\, teach
 es undergraduate and graduate instrumental conducting courses\, and serves
  as the director of the Big Red Basketball Band. Smedley earned a Doctor o
 f Musical Arts degree from the University of Washington and Master of Musi
 c and Bachelor of Music Education degrees from the Jacobs School of Music.
  He previously served on the music faculties of Boise State University and
  Western Kentucky University and as a public-school music educator in Coco
 a Beach\, Florida\; Santa Monica\, California\; and Kenosha\, Wisconsin. H
 e has conducted throughout North America and in Vietnam\, Poland\, Russia
 \, and Japan. Smedley maintains an active schedule as a clinician\, guest 
 conductor\, adjudicator\, and trumpet performer. His Symphonic Band was se
 lected to perform at the 2018 College Band Directors National Association 
 North Central Conference. He was a finalist at the 2023 Warsaw Wind Band C
 onducting Competition in Warsaw\, Poland. In 2025\, Navona Records release
 d the album Origins and Expansions\, featuring a composition by Kevin Bobo
 \, world-renowned steel pan soloist Liam Teague\, and the IU Wind Ensemble
 . Smedley’s research interests are varied and include projects in the ar
 eas of contemporary wind band literature\, wind band orchestration\, and c
 onducting pedagogy. Smedley is a member of the Gamma chapter of the intern
 ational band fraternity Phi Beta Mu and is an honorary member of Kappa Kap
 pa Psi\, Tau Beta Sigma\, and Phi Mu Alpha Sinfonia. He is a member of the
  College Band Directors National Association and the National Association 
 for Music Education. He lives in Bloomington\, Indiana\, with his wife\, J
 essica\, their daughter\, Ella\, and their Bedlington Terriers\, Piper and
  Finn.
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 201 S. Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, Indiana
  47405
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/symphonic-band-eric-m-sme
 dley-conductor-04-09-2026-14-25-53
X-SOURCE:WFIU Community Calendar
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/
END:VEVENT
