ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/59aa
 715/2147483647/strip/true/crop/2160x1080+0+0/resize/254x127!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8d%2Fd4%2F1dd22e3f4457a6
 55e646c2f34400%2Fbso-wethepeople.jpg
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Buskirk-Chumley Theater\nJoin the Bloomington Sym
 phony Orchestra as they perform a concert in recognition of our country’
 s 250th year. From the familiar square dance feel of Copland’s Hoedown\,
  to the soulful\, bluesy tonalities of Still’s Afro-American Symphony\, 
 this concert explores what it means to be an American.\n 4:15 pm pre-conce
 rt talk\n5:00 pm performance\n Program:\nAaron Copland – “Hoe-Down” 
 from Rodeo\nGary Powell Nash – “In Memoriam Sojourner Truth”\nJennif
 er Higdon – All Things Majestic\nWilliam Grant Still – Symphony No. 1
 \, “Afro-American”\n “I travel the world\, and I’m happy to say th
 at America is still the great melting pot – maybe a chunky stew rather t
 han a melting pot at this point\, but you know what I mean.” – Philip 
 Glass\, 1999 NPR interview\n BSO Season Passes can be purchased until Octo
 ber 16th. Passes include discounted tickets to all 4 season concerts\, res
 erved seating\, and other benefits. To learn more and purchase your Season
  Pass\, visit https://www.bloomingtonsymphony.com/seasonpass57/\nTickets: 
 https://buskirkchumley.org/events/we-the-people-november-1-2026/
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, Indi
 ana 47408
