 4a1881ffae4d7d%2Fwe-the-people-bso-nov-1-2026.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by Bloomington Symphony Orchestra\nOn Sunday\, Novem
 ber 1\, the Bloomington Symphony Orchestra\, in collaboration with the IU 
 Archives of African American Music and Culture\, will perform a concert in
  recognition of our country’s 250th year. From the familiar square dance
  feel of Aaron Copland’s Hoedown to the soulful\, bluesy tonalities of W
 illiam Grant Still’s Afro-American Symphony\, this concert explores what
  it means to be an American.\n Program:\n“Hoedown” from Rodeo – Aaro
 n Copland\n“In Memoriam Sojourner Truth” – Gary Powell Nash\nAll Thi
 ngs Majestic – Jennifer Higdon\nSymphony No. 1 – Afro-American Symphon
 y – William Grant Still\n 4:15 pm pre-concert talk with composer Gary Na
 sh\n5:00 pm performance\nTickets: https://buskirkchumley.org/events/we-the
 -people-november-1-2026/
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington\, Indi
 ana 47408
URL:https://www.ipm.org/community-calendar/event/we-the-people-08-10-2026-
 22-37-49
