UID:7d47ec74f47141231ce4445ad8a94ea5@ipm.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/2b2a
 c0b/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1080x1080+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F5a%2Fe6%2F5163b6254c83b8
 a8825d1397cf2c%2Fmobile-web-banner-1-1.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by WonderLab Science Museum\nWonderLab's Science of 
 Art series is teaming up with Discardia\, a project of the Center for Sust
 ainable Living\, for something a little different: Science of Art: Stitche
 d & Salvaged.\nTurns out mending is basically a science experiment in disg
 uise. Drop in and get hands-on with the math\, materials\, and hidden crea
 tivity behind fixing what's torn\, worn\, or written off too soon — and 
 discover how a needle and thread can be surprisingly powerful tools for bu
 ilding a more sustainable world.\nTickets: https://wonderlab.org/science-o
 f-art/
