ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims4/default/2be4
 48c/2147483647/strip/true/crop/1080x1080+0+0/resize/254x254!/quality/90/?u
 rl=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F8e%2F2f%2Fdadf1641404ca3
 f63d4e837f9fd1%2Fmobile-web-banner-1-1.png
DESCRIPTION:Presented by WonderLab Science Museum\nWonderLab is teaming up
  with the Bloomington Creative Glass Center for Science of Art: Glass Work
 ing — and things are about to get hot.\n Glass has a secret double life:
  it cuts\, melts\, and moves in ways that seem almost magical (spoiler: it
 's all science). Get hands-on with activities for all ages — try your ha
 nd at glass fusing\, create a mosaic to take home\, or discover the surpri
 sing\, sweet-toothed properties glass shares with sugar.\nTickets: https:/
 /wonderlab.org/science-of-art/
LOCATION:Wonderlab\, 308 W 4th St\, Bloomington\, Indiana 47401
